		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>Regulatory Natural Language Processing (Reg-NLP) is a multidisciplinary domain focused on facilitating access to and comprehension of regulatory documents and requirements. This paper outlines our strategy for creating a system to address the Regulatory Information Retrieval and Answer Generation (RIRAG) challenge, which was conducted during the Reg-NLP 2025 Workshop. The objective of this competition is to design a system capable of efficiently extracting pertinent passages from regulatory texts (ObliQA) and subsequently generating accurate, cohesive responses to inquiries related to compliance and obligations. Our proposed method employs a lightweight BM25 pre-filtering in retrieving relevant passages. This technique efficiently shortlisting candidates for subsequent processing with Transformer-based embeddings, thereby optimizing the use of resources.</p>
			</abstract>
